## Section: Bash Scripting

To pass this room:
---------------------------------------------------------------------

- The factory machines only work when the right functions are called.
- Process the assembly line using bash functions.

## Tasks:

1. Read assembly.txt - it contains 10 product codes.
   >> hint: `cat assembly.txt`

2. Write a script using functions to:
   - Validate: only process lines starting with "PROD-"
   - Extract: get the numeric part after "PROD-"
   - Sum all valid numeric IDs

   >> hint:
   >>   total=0
   >>   while IFS= read -r code; do
   >>     [[ "$code" == PROD-* ]] && total=$(( total + ${code#PROD-} ))
   >>   done < assembly.txt
   >>   echo $total

3. Run: ./getKey.sh <sum>
   >> hint: sum only the numeric parts of PROD-XX lines

>> To move to the next room: next PASSWORD

Good Luck !!!
